## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to unpack bit-packed fields without branches—a common low-level task in networking, codecs, and embedded systems.

## Key Concepts

- **Bitwise masks and shifts** extract subfields from packed integers efficiently
- **No branches** ensures constant-time execution, critical for performance-sensitive code
- **Endianness** is irrelevant when masking at exact bit positions

## Code Example

```c
typedef struct {
    uint8_t  version;
    uint8_t  type;
    uint16_t length;
    uint8_t  flags;
} Header;

Header extractHeaderFields(uint32_t w) {
    Header h;
    h.version = (w >> 28) & 0xF;  // Bits 31-28
    h.type    = (w >> 24) & 0xF;  // Bits 27-24
    h.length  = (w >> 8)  & 0xFFFF; // Bits 23-8
    h.flags   = w & 0xFF;          // Bits 7-0
    return h;
}
```

Each shift moves the target field to the least significant position, then the mask isolates the relevant bits. This approach is branchless, deterministic, and executes in constant time.

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to decompose a 128-bit operation into smaller parallel units and efficiently apply a well-known branchless counting technique.

## Key Concepts
- SWAR (SIMD Within A Register) popcount for 32-bit lanes
- 128-bit value decomposition into hi/lo components
- Branchless bit manipulation and final reduction

## Code Example
```c
unsigned int popcount32(unsigned int x) {
    x = x - ((x>>1)&0x55555555);
    x = (x&0x33333333)+((x>>2)&0x33333333);
    x = (x+(x>>4))&0x0F0F0F0F;
    return (x*0x01010101)>>24;
}

unsigned int popcount128(uint128 x) {
    return popcount32(x.lo) + popcount32(x.lo >> 32) + 
           popcount32(x.hi) + popcount32(x.hi >> 32);
}
```

## Quick Tests
```c
assert(popcount128(0) == 0);
assert(popcount128(UINT128_MAX) == 128);
assert(popcount128(0xF0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0) == 32);
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to implement a branchless, correct popcount in O(1) time, a common low-level optimization in performance-critical code (DBs, networking) at senior-level shops like Oracle and Twitter.

## Key Concepts
- Branchless bit counting
- Parallel bit manipulation with masks
- 32-bit mask progression and final accumulation

## Code Example
```c
uint32_t popcount32(uint32_t x){
  x = x - ((x >> 1) & 0x55555555);
  x = (x & 0x33333333) + ((x >> 2) & 0x33333333);
  x = (x + (x >> 4)) & 0x0F0F0F0F;
  x = x + (x >> 8);
  x = x + (x >> 16);
  return x & 0x3F;
}
```

